## The crew claim

Your resume prompt named 6 places. There were **25** — 20 saying "one crew" and **5 more telling the same lie in different words**: *"measured, formed and hung by our own crew"*, *"we fabricate, solder and hang it ourselves"*, *"the crew that measures your eave is the crew that puts the metal on it"*, *"siding, gutters and masonry run through the same crew"*, *"handled by the same crew in the same visit."* All rewritten to what's actually true — **one company, one contract, one project lead, one warranty, one clean site.** The honest uses on the About page (describing the industry failure mode you're *against*) stayed.

## So it can't come back

18 new banned regexes in **both** `build.py` and `tools/verify.py`. Proven, not asserted — I injected *"Colour matched by one crew; the phone is still being set up"* into a page and the build died naming all three, then restored it.

## One thing worth knowing

A bulk rule I wrote corrupted **`aria-labelledby` → `aria-labeledby`** across every page — a real accessibility break. **All four of your checkers passed it.** A word-level diff audit caught it before it shipped. That's now a standing rule in the addendum: no bulk text transform ships without one. I also made `mock-v2` a git repo (snapshot `0fd8b14` before any edit) — that's the only reason the audit was possible.

